title: Clarify that scheduler priority never bypasses `MaximumWeight`
doc:
  - audience: Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The documentation of `frame_support::traits::schedule::HARD_DEADLINE` stated that tasks of
      this priority or lower run in the block they ask for even if that exceeds the scheduler's
      `MaximumWeight`. `pallet-scheduler` has not behaved like that since the bounded scheduler
      rewrite: priority only orders the tasks of an agenda and a task that does not fit is
      postponed. The doc comment now describes the actual behaviour, and a regression test covers
      tasks of `HIGHEST_PRIORITY` and `HARD_DEADLINE` exceeding the weight limit.
crates:
  - name: frame-support
    bump: none
  - name: pallet-scheduler
    bump: none
